      "math_academy_id": "e-9099",
      "problem": "Consider a $8 \\times 6$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)) = 3,$ then find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A^T)).$",
      "worked_solution": "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14247906/assets/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=8,$ $n=6,$ and $n-r=3.$ \n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into $n-r=3,$ we can find the rank of $A{:}$\n\n$$\n6 - r = 3 \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nr = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T})) & =r=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
